---
import BaseLayout from '../components/BaseLayout.astro';
import Continue from '../components/Continue.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Understand"
  description="What a Digital Product Passport is, in plain language: the washing-machine story, one diagram, and who reads a passport."
  eyebrow="01 · Understand"
>
  <h1>What is a Digital Product Passport?</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A digital product passport is a record that travels with a thing — a washing machine, a
    battery, a spare part — and answers four questions: what is it, who made it, how do I
    repair it, and how do I recycle it.
  </p>

  <section aria-labelledby="story-heading">
    <h2 id="story-heading">A washing machine</h2>
    <p>
      Take a washing machine sold in 2026. On its frame, next to the rating plate, is a
      two-dimensional code. A consumer scans it with any phone camera. The code resolves to
      the machine's passport record, and the phone shows: the model and batch; who
      manufactured it and where; the energy class, with the test basis behind it; the list
      of spare parts, with disassembly instructions; and the take-back route — the nearest
      collection point, and which components to detach first.
    </p>
    <p>
      The same code serves other readers. A repairer sees the service history the
      manufacturer is required to publish. A customs officer sees the origin and conformity
      declarations their jurisdiction asks for. A recycler sees the material content, down
      to the parts that must be removed before shredding. One code, several readings: each
      reader sees the parts of the record that their role and their law give them.
    </p>
    <p>
      The record itself lives on servers, not on the machine. What lives on the machine is
      the carrier — the code — and a minimum of data that stays readable even with no
      network: what the product is, who operates the passport, and whether a recall is
      outstanding.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="plate" aria-labelledby="diagram-heading">
    <h2 id="diagram-heading">One diagram</h2>
    <p>
      A passport is data plus a way to reach it: a carrier on the product, a resolver that
      maps the code to the record, and the record with its readers around it.
    </p>
    <figure class="figure">
      <svg
        viewBox="0 0 780 340"
        role="img"
        aria-labelledby="learn-diagram-title learn-diagram-desc"
      >
        <title id="learn-diagram-title">
          From product to carrier to record, with four readers around the record
        </title>
        <desc id="learn-diagram-desc">
          A washing machine carries a two-dimensional code. The code resolves to a passport
          record. Four readers connect to the record: a consumer, a repairer, a customs
          officer, and a recycler, each reading the parts their role entitles them to.
        </desc>

        <!-- Product: washing machine -->
        <rect x="20" y="80" width="100" height="170" rx="8" class="box" />
        <rect x="35" y="95" width="70" height="10" rx="3" class="line-fill" />
        <circle cx="70" cy="185" r="30" class="outline" />
        <circle cx="70" cy="185" r="20" class="line-fill" />
        <rect x="35" y="140" width="16" height="24" rx="3" class="outline" />
        <rect x="89" y="140" width="16" height="24" rx="3" class="outline" />
        <text x="70" y="275" text-anchor="middle" class="lbl">Product</text>

        <!-- Arrow product -> carrier -->
        <line x1="128" y1="165" x2="168" y2="165" class="arrow" />
        <polygon points="168,160 178,165 168,170" class="arrow-head" />

        <!-- Carrier: the code -->
        <rect x="182" y="125" width="80" height="80" class="box" />
        <rect x="192" y="135" width="20" height="20" class="bold" />
        <rect x="232" y="135" width="20" height="20" class="bold" />
        <rect x="192" y="175" width="20" height="20" class="bold" />
        <rect x="224" y="167" width="8" height="8" class="bold" />
        <rect x="236" y="179" width="8" height="8" class="bold" />
        <rect x="206" y="181" width="8" height="8" class="bold" />
        <text x="222" y="275" text-anchor="middle" class="lbl">Carrier</text>

        <!-- Arrow carrier -> record -->
        <line x1="270" y1="165" x2="310" y2="165" class="arrow" />
        <polygon points="310,160 320,165 310,170" class="arrow-head" />

        <!-- Record: passport document -->
        <rect x="322" y="80" width="190" height="170" rx="6" class="box" />
        <rect x="340" y="98" width="120" height="12" rx="3" class="line-fill" />
        <line x1="340" y1="132" x2="494" y2="132" class="rule" />
        <line x1="340" y1="152" x2="480" y2="152" class="rule" />
        <line x1="340" y1="172" x2="494" y2="172" class="rule" />
        <line x1="340" y1="192" x2="460" y2="192" class="rule" />
        <circle cx="344" cy="222" r="4" class="ok-dot" />
        <line x1="356" y1="222" x2="440" y2="222" class="rule" />
        <text x="417" y="275" text-anchor="middle" class="lbl">Passport record</text>

        <!-- Readers -->
        <line x1="512" y1="70" x2="575" y2="70" class="rule" />
        <rect x="575" y="59" width="12" height="12" rx="2" class="bold" />
        <text x="595" y="66" class="lbl">Consumer</text>
        <text x="595" y="82" class="sub">repair and recycling information</text>

        <line x1="512" y1="145" x2="575" y2="145" class="rule" />
        <rect x="575" y="134" width="12" height="12" rx="2" class="bold" />
        <text x="595" y="141" class="lbl">Repairer</text>
        <text x="595" y="157" class="sub">service history, spare parts</text>

        <line x1="512" y1="220" x2="575" y2="220" class="rule" />
        <rect x="575" y="209" width="12" height="12" rx="2" class="bold" />
        <text x="595" y="216" class="lbl">Customs officer</text>
        <text x="595" y="232" class="sub">origin and conformity evidence</text>

        <line x1="512" y1="295" x2="575" y2="295" class="rule" />
        <rect x="575" y="284" width="12" height="12" rx="2" class="bold" />
        <text x="595" y="291" class="lbl">Recycler</text>
        <text x="595" y="307" class="sub">material content, take-back</text>
      </svg>
      <figcaption>
        Product, carrier, record, readers. The code on the product resolves to the record;
        each reader receives the view their role entitles them to.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="plate" aria-labelledby="readers-heading">
    <h2 id="readers-heading">Who reads one</h2>
    <dl class="readers">
      <div class="reader">
        <dt>Consumer</dt>
        <dd>What the product is, how long it should last, how to repair it, where it goes at end of life.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="reader">
        <dt>Repairer</dt>
        <dd>Spare-part lists, disassembly instructions, and the published service history.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="reader">
        <dt>Customs officer</dt>
        <dd>Origin and conformity evidence, in the form the jurisdiction of entry requires.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="reader">
        <dt>Recycler</dt>
        <dd>Material content, hazardous components, and take-back obligations.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <Continue
    href="/why/"
    num="02"
    title="Why an international core"
    desc="A single washing machine needs one passport. A product sold across borders meets several disclosure duties at once — and the question becomes whose passport it carries."
  />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .figure {
    margin: 1.4rem 0 0.4rem;
    max-width: none;
  }
  .figure svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }
  .figure figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 56ch;
  }
  .box {
    fill: #fff;
    stroke: var(--hairline);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }
  .outline {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--hairline);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }
  .line-fill {
    fill: var(--hairline);
    stroke: none;
  }
  .bold {
    fill: var(--navy);
    stroke: none;
  }
  .arrow {
    stroke: var(--muted);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }
  .arrow-head {
    fill: var(--muted);
  }
  .rule {
    stroke: var(--hairline);
    stroke-width: 2;
  }
  .ok-dot {
    fill: var(--green);
  }
  .lbl {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 13px;
    fill: var(--ink);
  }
  .sub {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 11px;
    fill: var(--muted);
  }

  .readers {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(13rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--hairline);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
    margin: 1.4rem 0 0;
    max-width: none;
  }
  .reader {
    background: var(--paper);
    padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
  }
  .reader dt {
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
  }
  .reader dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
</style>
